# Configuration and Infrastructure Standards

## YAML/TOML Files
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Use snake_case for keys
- Group related settings together
- Add comments for complex configurations
- Keep line length under 80 characters

## Docker Standards
- Use specific version tags, avoid `latest`
- Use multi-stage builds when possible
- Minimize the number of layers
- Use `.dockerignore` to exclude unnecessary files
- Use descriptive names for stages and images

## Shell Scripts
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Use snake_case for variable and function names
- Use UPPER_CASE for constants
- Add shebang line: `#!/bin/bash`
- Use `set -euo pipefail` for error handling
- Quote all variables: `"$variable"`

## Project Configuration Files
- [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Main Docker Compose configuration
- [docker-compose.dev.yml](mdc:docker-compose.dev.yml) - Development environment
- [Dockerfile](mdc:Dockerfile) - Main application container
- [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml) - Python project configuration
- [frontend/package.json](mdc:frontend/package.json) - Frontend dependencies
- [.pre-commit-config.yaml](mdc:.pre-commit-config.yaml) - Pre-commit hooks
